misc: hy310-motor: say what the driver is in Kconfig

The menu entry still describes the driver as focus adjustment. The stock
firmware has one motor node (hy310-board.dts:2635), one motor driver
(kallsyms c05d5c1c..c05d7d14) and no motor GPIOs beyond PH4..PH7 and PH14
(re/captures/HY310-DEV/stock_gpio_debug.txt), so there is no keystone motor
next to a focus motor -- this is the focus drive. The "EINT" rationale that
used to accompany the polling claim is dropped as well: the stock driver has
no interrupt path for the limiter at all, so polling was never a workaround
for anything.

The symbol name HY310_FOCUS_MOTOR is deliberately left alone so existing
defconfigs keep matching.

--- a/drivers/misc/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/misc/Kconfig
@@ -696,14 +696,17 @@
 
 
 config HY310_FOCUS_MOTOR
-	tristate "HY310 Focus Motor Driver"
+	tristate "HY310 projector stepper motor (focus drive)"
 	depends on OF && GPIOLIB
 	help
-	  Stepper motor driver for HY310 projector focus adjustment.
-	  Controls 4-phase stepper motor via GPIO with limit switch polling.
-	  Based on reverse engineering of the stock Allwinner H713 motor-control
-	  driver. Uses work-queue based async movement and DTS-configurable
-	  step tables.
+	  Driver for the single 4-phase GPIO stepper on the HY310 projector,
+	  which is its focus drive: the stock device tree has one motor node
+	  and the stock kernel one motor driver. Ported from the stock
+	  Allwinner motor-control driver. Movement runs in a work queue and
+	  the limit input is polled, as it is in stock; the step tables come
+	  from the device tree.
+
+	  If unsure, say N.
 endmenu
 source "drivers/misc/sunxi_tvtop/Kconfig"
 source "drivers/misc/sunxi_decd/Kconfig"
